Splits a rect along one axis. Allocation-free: constraints come in as a span (a collection
expression stays on the stack) and results go into a caller-provided span.

Span<Rect> rows = stackalloc Rect[3];
Layout.Vertical(area, [Constraint.Length(1), Constraint.Fill(), Constraint.Length(1)], rows);

Text with several styles: the text, runs that cover it from the start (each run's style is layered over
), and the base style for anything the runs don't cover. A view over caller memory,
so it costs nothing to build: runs are typically a collection expression on the stack, or come from a
 or .

buffer.SetText(x, y, new StyledText("j/k move", [new(3, keyStyle), new(5, dimStyle)]));

Builds a  into caller memory (usually stackalloc), merging adjacent runs
with the same style. Never throws when full: what fits is kept and  is set.

var keys = new StyledTextBuilder(stackalloc char[64], stackalloc StyledRun[8]);
keys.Append("j/k", key);
keys.Append(" move  ", dim);
keys.Append(count, key);
buffer.SetText(x, y, keys.Build());

An immediate-mode terminal session: alternate screen, raw input, double-buffered output.


Single-threaded: call ,  and 
from one thread.  may be called from any thread to wake the loop.


using var term = Terminal.Open();
while (running)
{
    if (!term.Poll(out Event ev, Timeout.Infinite)) continue;
    do { running = app.Handle(ev); } while (running && term.Poll(out ev, 0)); // coalesce bursts
    CellBuffer frame = term.BeginFrame();
    app.Render(frame);
    term.Present();                                                             // one write
}

